  "study_notes": {
    "observed": "Sep 2025 Seven Seas Ave (SSE and WSW): five-storey white slab with paired windows and blue stair towers at its corners; official Job Corps aerial: E-shaped plan of equal height; entrance photo: glazed doors under a flat canopy. The official entrance photo (hero.jpg, '369 / 275 California Ave') shows the glazed doors under the flat canopy of the one-storey entrance wing at the SSE end (the low wing in 369-sideC_151 and the jc-07 aerial), outside this footprint; the Sep 2025 WSW photo (369-sideD_241) shows no entrance on the WSW wing face, so the lobby entry modelled there was removed (2026-10-24 grid batch B1). L3 (2026-11-18): Sep 2025 sideD/spec/sideC, hero.jpg and the owner's 2026-11-18 window and telephoto photos: pale putty walls; slate stair towers with one two-pane light per half landing on their sides, about 1 m over the wing roof; eyebrow sunshades over the wide groups on storeys 1-3 of the WSW and SSE faces (also over the SSE ground floor, <=2018 photo) and on the north part of the middle wing's WSW face (telephoto); dark glass with white sashes and blinds; a thin overhanging roof slab with a blue-green fascia and underside; sand-framed ground bays with slate panels on the WSW face; lilac-grey set-back strips beside the towers; the SSE face starts with two wide groups at the SW corner; the NW tower (west wing's NNW end) carries an antenna cluster at the 4th floor and a round duct to a gooseneck hood; penthouse, siren mast and grey-brown roofs (jc-07).",
    "inferred": "Five storeys over the OSM 6 m tag, window cadence, doors on the other accessible sides; the SSE spine wall faces the attached Oasis hall (no door). Stair towers are enclosed blocks (no stairs modelled). L3: hood, slab, band, tower-light and equipment sizes, the SSE columns past u 31.4, the middle wing's photographed column station, the penthouse size and its plant annex, tanks and roof units (jc-07, undated), and the duct and cluster layout are production_inference; the east and middle NNW towers take colour and height only (jc-08, telephoto); the SE tower keeps its windows (no dated photo since the repaint).",
    "footprint": "Frozen 32-edge E plan split into the spine-and-wings block, the west and east wing ends, the SW and SE corner towers and the three NNW end towers (the middle wing's end block is its tower). The NW tower's WSW side is 1.9 m deep in OSM against about 3 m in the owner's telephoto; the frozen footprint stands."
  },
